    "faq_JPpizx": {
      "type": "faq",
      "blocks": {
        "question_q4wELk": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "heading": "How Does TRICARE Cover Breast Pumps?",
            "text": "<p>TRICARE may cover one breast pump per birth, along with select breastfeeding supplies. Coverage applies to active-duty service members, military spouses, and dependents under TRICARE Prime, TRICARE Select, and other TRICARE plans. Check with your insurance representative to be sure what is covered under your plan.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_Lz7pyL": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "heading": "Is There a Cost for Military Moms to Get a Breast Pump?",
            "text": "<p>In most cases, TRICARE and other military insurance providers cover the full cost of a new breast pump. Some plans may require a prescription or minor out-of-pocket costs, but our team will help you navigate the process to minimize expenses.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_J7hNmL": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "heading": "What Documents Are Needed for Military Breast Pump Approval?",
            "text": "<p>Most military insurance providers require:</p><ul><li>Proof of TRICARE coverage</li><li>A prescription from a healthcare provider</li><li>Basic personal and military service details</li></ul><p>Our team will assist you in gathering and submitting all required paperwork to make the approval process as smooth as possible.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_hTjYkK": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "heading": "When Can I Order My Breast Pump?",
            "text": "<p>You can request your pump anytime during pregnancy or after birth. TRICARE allows moms to receive their pump as early as the third trimester to ensure they’re prepared before the baby arrives.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_TLqVmB": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "heading": "How Long Does It Take to Get My Breast Pump?",
            "text": "<p>Once all required documents are submitted, most military moms receive their breast pump within a few business days. Ameda works quickly to process your order so you can start your breastfeeding journey without delay.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
